{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "T21-1e: `var n: u32 = <int lane>` admits its initializer through the inline u32 range check (ge 0 / le 4294967295 on the lane register) because the declaration site declares the initializer's VALUE_REP_INT_LANE witness to the boundary. After ca574c869 retired the MIR_reg_type probe (D2.4.1) the witness was never passed, so every such declaration boxed the lane, spilled it, and called lambda_type_check -- on crypto_sha1 that was every SHA round (3x, Result36). The in-range path may not call it. LR03-11 (2026-09-25): the cold reject arm calls lambda_type_check exactly once per boundary so a rejection carries its E201 diagnostic (S11.4.1v3); the range branch jumps past it, so the call follows the bt and is counted.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_rol_#",
      "count": {
        "call\tlambda_type_check_p, lambda_type_check": 1
      },
      "expect_seq": [
        { "pattern": "ge\t{{r}}, %p1, 0" },
        { "pattern": "le\t{{r}}, %p1, 4294967295" },
        { "pattern": "bt\tL" },
        { "pattern": "call\tlambda_type_check_p, lambda_type_check" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "in_func": "_safe_add_#",
      "count": {
        "call\tlambda_type_check_p, lambda_type_check": 2
      },
      "expect": [
        "le\t{{r}}, {{r}}, 4294967295"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
